  === Complete Solutions
  #sol-item(1, "C", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    *Dusk*, and the title is a mood rather than a time of day: the assembly takes place in the morning.
  ]

  #sol-item(2, "C", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    He breaks down, drops the microphone and is heard to say *Save me, O God!* The resignation is not announced until five days later, in Chapter 2.
  ]
  ]

  #sol-item(3, "D", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Mrs Grace Apeh, the vice principal. The MD is not at the assembly and arrives at half past nine; Ope Wande and Audu are not called until later.
  ]

  #sol-item(4, "C", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Mr Justus Anabel, the chemistry teacher. The other three are real members of staff, which is what makes the question a memory test.
  ]

  #sol-item(5, "A", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Half past nine — she was at an event outside the school when the vice principal called her.
  ]

  #sol-item(6, "A", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Mr Ope Wande, physics teacher and pastor. Audu is the comic relief, Amos the accountant, and Egi Meko belongs to Bepo's previous school.
  ]

  #sol-item(7, "C", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    About ten minutes, and it produces nothing — which is the point of the scene: the problem is not a problem of counsel.
  ]

  #sol-item(8, "A", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Five days later, in Chapter 2. The interval is the whole of *The Enticement*'s opening, and it is the commonest trap in the section.
  ]

  #sol-item(9, "D", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    *The Enticement* — the case for going, made by the figures and by the people around him.
  ]

  #sol-item(10, "C", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Twenty-four years, from headmaster of Stardom Kiddies to principal of the secondary school.
  ]

  #sol-item(11, "C", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Stardom Kiddies, the nursery and primary arm of the same school. Beesway and Fruitful Future belong to his earlier career.
  ]

  #sol-item(12, "A", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    About £3,600 a month, against Seri's £10,000 as a nurse. The two figures are quoted together to show that the arithmetic is not as simple as it looks.
  ]

  #sol-item(13, "B", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    *Migration Tales* — the stories of those who have gone, told by colleagues and friends.
  ]

  #sol-item(14, "B", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Sola, now settled in the United Kingdom. Jare and Hope are the cautionary tales, and Nku is the member of staff who took a loan and disappeared.
  ]

  #sol-item(15, "A", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Caring for an elderly couple — the banking job he left Nigeria for had nothing to do with the work he found.
  ]

  #sol-item(16, "A", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    His wife, who had funded his master's degree, stopped providing for him after a few months.
  ]

  #sol-item(17, "C", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    About a thousand — a third of the country's doctors, which is the figure the chapter uses to measure the drain.
  ]

  #sol-item(18, "B", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Mr Nku. The story is told in Chapter 3 as one of the desperate ways people fund the ticket.
  ]

  #sol-item(19, "B", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    *A Case of Visa Denied*, and the case belongs to the Ignatius family.
  ]

  #sol-item(20, "B", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Mrs Ignatius. Mrs Ladele is the parent of Bibi, whose nightmares end Mr Ayesoro's teaching career.
  ]

  #sol-item(21, "C", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    One of the three — Favour, the SSS2 pupil at Stardom — was not his, and he ordered mother and daughter out of the house.
  ]

  #sol-item(22, "B", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    *Snake in the Roof*, from the chairman's proverb about the staff cooperative.
  ]

  #sol-item(23, "B", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Cars parked on school land. The investigation that follows finds no theft, only a cooperative that has lent its members money.
  ]

  #sol-item(24, "B", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    About ₦95 million. ₦250,000 is the cap the board later places on a single loan, and ₦2 million is the loan Nku took.
  ]

  #sol-item(25, "D", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Cap loans at ₦250,000. The cooperative survives, diminished — which is exactly what the chairman intended.
  ]

  #sol-item(26, "B", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    A snake hung in the roof: a danger you have housed yourself and sleep beneath.
  ]

  #sol-item(27, "B", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    The title is the sentence the chapter turns on, printed with both verb forms.
  ]

  #sol-item(28, "A", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    *Ade as well as Jide comes early*, and the verb is correct: where subjects are joined by *as well as*, the verb agrees with the first.
  ]

  #sol-item(29, "B", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Mr Guta, who found the sentence in his son's note and threatened to withdraw his children.
  ]

  #sol-item(30, "D", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    *Ritualists* — and the chapter is a memory of Beesway, not a scene in the present.
  ]

  #sol-item(31, "D", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    A cow, buried alive. The scene is the reason he left Beesway, and it is recalled rather than witnessed in the present of the novel.
  ]

  #sol-item(32, "A", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Mr Egi Meko. Ogo is the parent at Fruitful Future, Guta the complaining parent at Stardom, and Ogba the father in the lawsuit.
  ]

  #sol-item(33, "C", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    More than seventy pupils by its third session — and then failed when the roads went bad and the fee-paying families moved away.
  ]

  #sol-item(34, "A", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    ₦35,000. Bepo refuses, the parent withdraws his child, and years later the same man is arrested for murdering a client.
  ]

  #sol-item(35, "C", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    *Missions Unaccomplished* — the feud, the election and the invention club Bepo will not see finished.
  ]

  #sol-item(36, "A", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Banky and Tosh. Favour and Bibi are pupils from other chapters, and Nike and Kike are Bepo's children.
  ]

  #sol-item(37, "A", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    ₦50,000, with deputies at ₦40,000 and other posts at ₦25,000. The sums are the chapter's quiet joke about school politics.
  ]

  #sol-item(38, "A", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    *Laughing Waterfalls*, from the excursions that end at Badagry.
  ]

  #sol-item(39, "C", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Badagry — the Akran's palace, the First Storey Building and the Black Heritage Museum. The waterfalls are earlier in the same chapter.
  ]

  #sol-item(40, "B", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Chapter 10, *Passport Pains*, and the office he attends is in Ibadan.
  ]

